From 9feef866b1050bde8dfbaa79d6166a21f110c6ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 19:03:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Export tap patterns, macros, combos and mod-morphs to MoErgo
 JSON

snapshot_to_moergo_json wrote only what a VIA keycode can carry, so a
layout with a morse (TD(n)), a macro, an autoshift tap-hold or several
USER keys could not be exported at all, and a profiled tap-hold lost its
timing silently. Export now writes the editor definitions the import
lowers back to the same runtime values (moergo/raise.rs, the inverse of
lower.rs):

- TD(n) tap/hold as a hold-tap: modifier/key (bilateral ones with the
  other hand's hold-trigger-key-positions), layer/key, autoshift over a
  shift macro, sticky modifier over a &sticky_key; taps-only as a
  tap-dance.
- MT/LT/TH with a named morse profile as a hold-tap carrying its timing.
- MACRO(n) as a macro; forks as mod-morphs on the keys they rewrite;
  the snapshot's combos (LMT as the window-switcher macro).
- USER keys mapped where MoErgo has an equivalent; every binding that
  has none is listed with its location and reason, all at once.
- A template's definitions are reused by content, never repeated; the
  ones its keymap used and the export replaced are removed, so a
  re-import does not drop layers a stale home-row-mod macro names.

Import mirrors it: tapDances are read, a &kp/&kp hold-tap is a mod-tap,
a &mo hold-tap may restrict its hold by position, a mod-morph or
tap-dance step may name a custom behavior, and a combo's &to is TO
(as on a key) rather than DF.

Tests: TailorKey bilateral and Engrammer exports round-trip to the same
snapshot with and without a template, and re-export over their own
output is unchanged; TailorKey for RMK's TOML round-trips key for key
apart from the 13 bindings ZMK has no equivalent for, which the export
names.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QpAvhekAu35RCnRCUtmvDL
